---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Draft Omen"
  description="Learn who maintains Draft Omen, why it stays read-only, and which services provide its card and draft data."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">About the project</p>
      <h1>A calm companion for complicated picks.</h1>
      <p class="intro-lede">
        Draft Omen is an unofficial project by <strong>Andrea Grandi</strong>.
        It is made for drafters who want useful context while keeping the final
        pick—and the play experience—in their own hands.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section pt-0" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
    <div class="shell content-grid">
      <aside class="content-aside">
        <p class="eyebrow">The short version</p>
        <h2 class="content-heading">Read-only by design.</h2>
        <p>
          Draft Omen watches a local log and presents guidance. It does not read
          the screen, send game input, or automate MTG Arena.
        </p>
      </aside>

      <div class="content-stack">
        <section id="about-heading">
          <h2>What Draft Omen is</h2>
          <p>
            Draft Omen follows MTG Arena Quick, Premier, Traditional and Pick-Two
            drafts through Arena's local{" "}
            <code>Player.log</code>. It identifies offered packs and picks, joins
            card metadata to public data, and keeps the score inputs visible as a
            draft develops. When the draft is complete, it can propose a 40-card
            build that you recreate in Arena yourself.
          </p>
          <p>
            Andrea Grandi maintains the Python application, its terminal and
            desktop interfaces, and the methodology documentation in the{" "}
            <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/andreagrandi/draftomen">public repository</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="ack-heading">
          <h2 id="ack-heading">Acknowledgments</h2>
          <p>
            Card identity and card details are supported by{" "}
            <a class="text-link" href="https://scryfall.com/">Scryfall</a>.{" "}
            Draft statistics and color-pair context come from{" "}
            <a class="text-link" href="https://www.17lands.com/">17Lands</a>.{" "}
            Their data makes the recommendation context possible; neither service
            endorses Draft Omen.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="status-heading">
          <h2 id="status-heading">Unofficial status</h2>
          <div class="disclaimer">
            <p>
              Draft Omen is not affiliated with, sponsored by, approved by, or endorsed by Wizards of the Coast, Scryfall, or 17Lands.<br /><br />
              Draft Omen is unofficial Fan Content permitted under the Fan Content Policy. Not approved/endorsed by Wizards. Portions of the materials used are property of Wizards of the Coast. ©Wizards of the Coast LLC. Card data from Scryfall and 17Lands; neither service endorses this tool.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
